### 🧵 2.5 Graphiti — Temporal Knowledge-Graph Memory

🔗 [Graphiti on GitHub](https://github.com/getzep/graphiti)

Traditional RAG:
```
Documents → Chunk → Embed → Vector DB → Similarity search → Retrieve
```

Graphiti instead builds a **temporally-aware knowledge graph** — it tracks not just facts, but *when* they were true and what changed:

```
January: Database = MongoDB
March:   Database = PostgreSQL
June:    Database = Supabase
```

A flat memory store might retrieve conflicting facts. A temporal graph asks: *what was true, when, and what's current?*

**Token impact:**

| Approach | Context sent |
|---|---|
| Dump entire project history | ~500,000 tokens |
| Graphiti retrieves only relevant facts | ~3,000 tokens |

> The goal isn't *more* context — it's *better* context.

