### 🅶️ 5.8 Perplexity — A Search System, Not a Coding Model

Perplexity = model + retrieval + citations + research workflow (Sonar family). Best for research, documentation discovery, and source-grounded answers — **not** a raw coding-model substitute.

---

### 🅷️ 5.9 Cursor, Lovable & Antigravity — Orchestration Layers

**Cursor** = model orchestration layer, not a model itself. It routes across GPT/Claude/Gemini/Grok/its own Composer model based on cost/balance/intelligence settings. The real intelligence of "using Cursor" = model + repo indexing + context selection + terminal + agent loop + error feedback — a weaker model with excellent context/verification can beat a stronger model given bad prompts and no tests.

**Lovable** = AI application-building product, best for prototypes/MVPs; deep custom architecture eventually needs a full IDE workflow.

**Antigravity** = Google's agentic platform layered on Gemini models.

**Claude Code** = Claude model + terminal + filesystem + planning + agent loop + project instructions (AGENTS.md-style).

> **Key takeaway:** comparing "Claude vs. Cursor" is like comparing an engine to a car — one is a model, the other is a system built around models.

