```
CPU  → application logic, orchestration, scheduling (flexible, less parallel)
GPU  → massively parallel matrix ops — training & inference (NVIDIA's core strength)
TPU  → Google's custom tensor hardware, powers much of Gemini
NPU  → small local AI on laptops/phones/edge devices
```

**What we genuinely don't know:** exact watts-per-request for any specific GPT/Claude/Gemini call — that depends on GPU count, batch size, MoE routing, precision, context length, and utilization, none of which providers disclose per-request. Any specific "X model uses Y watts" claim online should be treated skeptically.

**Why long context isn't free:** 1M-token context windows require much larger KV-cache/attention memory — sending huge context by default (rather than retrieving what's relevant) hurts cost, latency, *and* memory efficiency.

