## 7. Recommended Learning Path

```
Tier 1 — Understand agentic coding
   → Cline, Roo Code, Reticle
   Study: file inspection, tool selection, context maintenance,
          command execution, error recovery, completion verification

Tier 2 — Learn memory & context engineering
   → Graphiti, Anthropic's context-engineering guidance
   Study: vector retrieval, hybrid retrieval, knowledge graphs,
          temporal data, compaction, context selection

Tier 3 — Learn local/open models
   → Ollama
   Study: local inference, coding models, embeddings, model routing

Tier 4 — Learn quality & review
   → CodeRabbit, Reticle, test frameworks, browser automation, CI/CD
   Study: generate → review → test → observe → fix
```

**Hands-on build order:**
```
1. Install Ollama, experiment with local models
2. Use an agent (Cline / Roo Code)
3. Write a real AGENTS.md for a test project
4. Add MCP tools selectively
5. Add Reticle for runtime verification
6. Add automated tests
7. Add CodeRabbit for review
8. Try a Ralph-style implementation loop
9. Later: add Graphiti or another memory layer
```

**If you implement only three things, prioritize:**
1. `AGENTS.md` + persistent decision/architecture files
2. Task checkpoints / context compaction for long-running work
3. A strict implement → targeted test → failure-feedback loop

